Tab Exit [Interface]
Select to which of its successors the object moves the MU on the tab Exit.
Remarks
Note
If Plant Simulation determines the n-th successor of an object, for example with print
MyStation.succ(n) and if the n-th successor is an Interface, Plant Simulation does not return the
Interface itself, but any successor of the Interface according to the Exit strategy of the Interface.
If you select a non-blocking exit strategy, Plant Simulation returns the next available successor
according to the exit strategy or it returns VOID, when no successor can receive parts.
When the Interface has a single successor, Plant Simulation returns this successor, even if you selected
a non-blocking exit strategy and if the successor is occupied or failed/paused.
The Interface shows the number of the next selected exit (next Aimed Successor) provided you already
determined it, for example by calling the method succ for the successor object.
Compare the sample models: Click the Window ribbon tab, click Start Page > Getting Started > Example
Models > Small Examples. Then, select the respective Category, the Topic, and the Example in the
dialog Examples Collection, and click Open Model.
